        <mxCell id="keyInsight" value="Centralizing Alertmanager creates risk: a single bad inhibit rule could silence another team&#39;s critical alerts.&#10;&#10;Four guardrails make this STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE — not just discouraged by convention, but blocked at the&#10;label/CI/routing level. Team A&#39;s alerts cannot silence Team B&#39;s, even with a shared Alertmanager." style="text;html=1;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;fontSize=10;fontColor=#0F2A47;" vertex="1" parent="1">
